From c864fa6b5af4a11ee2d0ba65df908c54c1a6b1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Try Omarchy Release <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:29:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Expose the Windows camera to the guest as a V4L2 device

Port the macOS on-demand camera bridge to Windows. The guest reads the same
framed NV12 stream, but over a virtio-serial port the launcher backs with a
host-side chardev instead of a macOS-native socket, and writes it to a
v4l2loopback camera at /dev/video42 that applications see as "Windows Camera".
The guest asks the host to start capture only while a consumer holds the camera
open. Adds v4l2loopback-dkms and linux-headers to the guest and carries the
bridge through compatibility revision 24.
